stanzas:
Outside the window, bullfinches
Warm the rowan bush;
Its plump berries glow red against the snow.

I have a family of my own;
My life's course was set long ago,
And yet I can't fool myself, however hard I try.

Outside the window, bullfinches
Warm the rowan bush;
Its plump berries glow red against the snow.

